# Ctrl+D on an empty input line exits (internal/tui/keys.go Router's
# ctrl+d case: HasInput() false -> Exit()). On a non-empty line Ctrl+D is
# left to the editor as delete-forward instead (not exercised here — that
# is ordinary editing, not an exit).
@faux testdata/faux/hello.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT before-ctrl-d
KEY ctrl+d
WAIT 1
SHOT after-ctrl-d
NOTE kiln should have exited; nothing further to type
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
